@startuml data-model
title Class diagram — Express Voitures (data model)

hide circle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor White
  BorderColor #34495E
  ArrowColor #34495E
}

class Brand {
  -id : Integer
  -name : String
}

class CarModel {
  -id : Integer
  -name : String
}

class Vehicle {
  -id : Integer
  -vin : String [0..1]
  -year : Integer
  -trim : String [0..1]
  -purchaseDate : Date
  -purchasePrice : Decimal
  -availabilityDate : Date [0..1]
  -saleDate : Date [0..1]
  -description : String [0..1]
  -photoUrl : String [0..1]
  --
  +/repairsCost : Decimal
  +/salePrice : Decimal
  +/isAvailable : Boolean
}

class Repair {
  -id : Integer
  -description : String
  -cost : Decimal
}

class IdentityUser <<ASP.NET Identity>> #EEEEEE {
  -id : String
  -email : String
}

note right of Vehicle
  {A Vehicle is one **physical unit** in stock,
  not a catalogue category.}

  {salePrice = purchasePrice + repairsCost + 500 EUR}
  {salePrice, repairsCost and isAvailable are derived:
  computed on read, never stored as columns}

  {saleDate empty = still for sale}
end note

note bottom of Repair
  {A Repair is a first-class entity: the client's
  spreadsheet packed several repairs into one cell,
  which is not atomic.}
end note

note right of IdentityUser
  {Single manager account. No association with the
  inventory: one user administers everything.}
end note

note left of Vehicle
  {trim stays a plain attribute rather than an
  entity: the 7 vehicles of the client's inventory
  have 7 distinct trims (LE, Sport, TCe, XLT, LX,
  S, SEL) and share none, so a table would
  deduplicate nothing. Brand is a table because
  "Ford" appears twice.}
end note

note left of Brand
  {name is unique}
end note

note right of CarModel
  {(brand, name) is unique}
end note

Brand "1" -- "0..*" CarModel : offers >
CarModel "1" -- "0..*" Vehicle : stocked as >
Vehicle "1" *-- "0..*" Repair : undergoes >

legend bottom right
  |= Notation |= Meaning |
  | 1 | exactly one |
  | 0..1 | zero or one (optional) |
  | 0..* | zero to many |
  | / | derived attribute, not persisted |
  | filled diamond | composition: the part cannot exist without the whole |
  Read a multiplicity at the end //opposite// the class you start from.
  Foreign keys are not shown as attributes: the associations carry them.
endlegend

@enduml
